City Clerk		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         Mission Statement The City Clerk is the City's chief election officer and head of the City's Department of Records, which includes City archives and vital records, and custodian of the city seal. The City Clerk administers the oath of office to City officials and performs all the duties of a municipal clerk as authorized under Massachusetts General Laws. Methuen residents can transact routine City Clerk business in our Customer Service Center located in the Searles Building or by using the online payment system. Please note that cash payments are no longer accepted.  Please note :  Payments must be made by check or credit/debit card. Credit/Debit card issuers may charge users an additional fee for credit/debit payments. If you are interested in becoming an election worker, please  email City Clerk  or call City Clerk Anne Drouin at 978-983-8515. To qualify, you must be a registered voter in Massachusetts. For useful voter information and forms, please view the  Secretary of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts - Elections page . Questions in regard to the new House and Senate districts can be found on the  Secretary of State's website . If you need further clarification please call the Clerk's Office at 978-983-8515. 
     

 
